      "updated": 1783056153395,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "(i) Inline CSS\n(ii) Internal CSS\n(iii) External CSS\n(iv) @import(url)\n\n(i) Inline CSS : Applying the CSS in the same line by using style attrinute\n                   is known as inline CSS.\n\n(ii) Internal CSS : Applying the CSS using style tag, in the head tag of \n                       HTML is known as internal CSS.\n\n(iii) External CSS : Creating a seperate CSS file with CSS extension,\n                        and then we have to link that CSS file in HTML by \n                        using link tag, inside the tag is known as external CSS.\n\n(iv) @import(url) : It is used for importing multiple CSS file inside one \n                       CSS file.\n \nPriority : Inline > > Internal > > External CSS.\n\nSelector are used to target an html so that we can applys properties \ntypes of selector :\nsimple selector \ncombinator\nattribute \npseudo class selector\npseudo element selector\ngroup selector\n\nsimple selector : id , class, tagname , element, grouping, universal selector that main or element selector\n\ncombinator selector : descendent, child and immedeate / adjecent selector \ngenral sibling selector \n\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "(i) Inline CSS\n(ii) Internal CSS\n(iii) External CSS\n(iv) @import(url)\n\n(i) Inline CSS : Applying the CSS in the same line by using style attrinute\n                   is known as inline CSS.\n\n(ii) Internal CSS : Applying the CSS using style tag, in the head tag of \n                       HTML is known as internal CSS.\n\n(iii) External CSS : Creating a seperate CSS file with CSS extension,\n                        and then we have to link that CSS file in HTML by \n                        using link tag, inside the tag is known as external CSS.\n\n(iv) @import(url) : It is used for importing multiple CSS file inside one \n                       CSS file.\n \nPriority : Inline > > Internal > > External CSS.\n\nSelector are used to target an html so that we can applys properties \ntypes of selector :\nsimple selector \ncombinator\nattribute \npseudo class selector\npseudo element selector\ngroup selector\n\nsimple selector : id , class, tagname , element, grouping, universal selector that main or element selector\n\ncombinator selector : descendent, child and immedeate / adjecent selector \ngenral sibling selector \n\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
